@startuml
!theme plain
|a1| Operator
|a1|
start
:Rental Items are Returned to the Store;
:v1: Return method ({Customer returns items, Delivery picks up}); <<objectSignal>>
if () then ([v1 = 'Customer returns items'])
:Customer returns the items to the store;
else ([v1 = 'Delivery picks up'])
:Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site;
endif
:Items are counted and compared to the original contract;
:v2: Order status ({Complete, Incomplete, Damaged}); <<objectSignal>>
switch ()
case ([v2 = 'Complete'])
:Order is complete and all items were returned;
:Items are packed for an existing order;
:Email customer missing items and replacement charges;
:Customer returns the missing items;
case ([v2 = 'Incomplete'])
:Order is incomplete and items are missing;
:Items are stored for future orders;
:Temporarily take damaged items out of inventory;
:Customer does not return the missing items;
case ([v2 = 'Damaged'])
:Order is complete but items are damaged;
:Items are packed for an existing order;
:Email customer damaged items and additional charges;
endswitch
:Finally, when the process is complete, it ends;
:v3: Repair status ({Repaired, Discarded}); <<objectSignal>>
if () then ([v3 = 'Repaired'])
:Items are repaired and added into inventory;
else ([v3 = 'Discarded'])
:Items can't be repaired and are discarded;
endif
:Lastly, the items are packed for an existing order;
:v4: Disposition ({Packed, Stored}); <<objectSignal>>
if () then ([v4 = 'Packed'])
:Items are packed for an existing order;
else ([v4 = 'Stored'])
:Items are stored for future orders;
endif
:Once again, when the process is complete, it ends;
:Email customer with replacement charges;
stop
@enduml